# Trivy ignore list — accepted container-image findings
#
# Consumed by the "Fail on CRITICAL image vulnerabilities" step in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml, which gates on CRITICAL severity with
# `ignore-unfixed: true`.
#
# SCOPE OF THE GATE
#   - Only CRITICAL findings block. HIGH and below are still reported to the
#     Security tab by the advisory SARIF scan in the same job, but do not fail CI.
#   - Only *fixable* findings block. A CVE with no upstream fix available is not
#     actionable in a pull request, so `ignore-unfixed` filters it out. It will
#     start blocking automatically once a fixed version ships — which is the
#     point at which someone can actually do something about it.
#
# ADDING AN ENTRY
#   An entry here is a deliberate, temporary acceptance of a known CRITICAL
#   vulnerability. It is not a way to make CI quiet. Every entry MUST carry:
#
#     1. The CVE id, one per line, uncommented.
#     2. Why it is not exploitable in this image, or why the fix cannot be taken.
#     3. A machine-enforced expiry using Trivy's classic syntax:
#          CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#        Comment-only "Expires:" lines are documentation and are NOT enforced.
#     4. A link to the tracking issue or spec.
#
#   Format:
#
#     # CVE-2026-12345 — <package> <version>
#     # Rationale: <why this does not affect this image>
#     # Tracking:  https://github.com/ianshank/Strategos-MCTS/issues/<n>
#     CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# An empty list is the correct steady state. If this file grows, that is a signal
# the base image needs updating, not that the gate needs loosening.
#
# Charter note: CHARTER.md NG-3 requires claims to be reproducible. Reproduce the
# gate locally with:
#
#   docker build -t langgraph-mcts:test --target production .
#   trivy image --severity CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed \
#     --ignorefile .trivyignore --exit-code 1 langgraph-mcts:test
#
# --- accepted findings below this line ---
#
# CVE-2025-23042 (gradio <5.11) was previously listed with a comment-only expiry
# of 2026-09-04. The production image on main already resolved gradio 5.38.2
# (CI Pipeline run 34705825904), which includes that fix, so the ignore is gone.
# Do not re-add it. The 2026-09-12 red docker-build job was perl-base on Debian
# 13 (CVE-2026-13221, CVE-2026-42496, CVE-2026-8376) — upgrade the package; do
# not ignore those CVEs.
